                "required": [
                  "cmd",
                  "cwd",
                  "returncode",
                  "stdout",
                  "stderr",
                  "duration_ms",
                  "executor"
                ],
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "description": "Retour du mode D\u00c9TACH\u00c9 de ``execute_shell`` (``background=True``).\n\nSon retour (``ok/background/pid/cmd/log/hint``) ne satisfait ni\n``ExecuteShellResult`` (qui exige cwd/returncode/stdout/stderr/duration_ms/\nexecutor) ni ``ErrEnvelope`` (qui exige ``ok: false``) : sans cette branche\nde l'``outputSchema``, la validation de sortie du serveur MCP l\u00e8verait\nAPR\u00c8S le lancement du processus, et le mod\u00e8le relancerait un processus\nd\u00e9tach\u00e9 en double. Un mod\u00e8le D\u00c9DI\u00c9 plut\u00f4t qu'un assouplissement\nd'``ExecuteShellResult`` : le chemin normal garde son sch\u00e9ma strict.",
                "properties": {
                  "ok": {
                    "const": true,
                    "default": true,
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "background": {
                    "default": true,
                    "description": "Always true: the process was detached.",
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "pid": {
                    "description": "PID of the detached process, inside the container.",
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "cmd": {
                    "description": "The shell command that was launched.",
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "log": {
                    "description": "Container path of the file collecting stdout/stderr.",
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "hint": {
                    "default": "",
                    "description": "How to read the log and how to stop the process.",
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "pid",
                  "cmd",
                  "log"
                ],
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "description": "Typed shape of the error envelope produced by ``_toolkit.err()``.\n\nMirrors the error contract the chat frontend parses :\n  * ``ok`` is the discriminator (False = failure),\n  * ``error`` is a stable machine code (snake_case),\n  * ``message`` is the human-readable text,\n  * ``fix`` is an optional hint how to recover.\n\nTools declare their return type as ``Union[<SuccessModel>,\nErrEnvelope]`` so FastMCP generates a discriminated union schema\nthe LLM can pattern-match on the ``ok`` field. The runtime\nwire format is unchanged \u2014 both branches serialise to the same\nJSON dict the frontend already reads.\n\n``extra='allow'`` because ``err()`` lets each call site attach\ncontext (``cmd``, ``path``, ``expected``, ``actual``, \u2026) \u2014 these\nare kept for the LLM but aren't part of the strict schema.",
                "properties": {
                  "ok": {
                    "const": false,
                    "default": false,
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "error": {
                    "description": "Stable machine code (e.g. 'not_found', 'too_large').",
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "message": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Human-readable error message."
                  },
                  "fix": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Suggested recovery action."
                  },
                  "next_action": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "Concrete next tool/arg to try."
                  },
                  "retryable": {
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "boolean"
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "True iff a retry might succeed (transient error)."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "error"
                ],
                "type": "object"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "result"
        ],
        "type": "object",
        "x-fastmcp-wrap-result": true
      },
